<Article
  title="Catan Development Card Rules: One Per Turn? Before Rolling?"
  description="You can play one development card per turn, before or after you roll, but never on the turn you bought it. Every Catan dev card timing rule, answered."
  game="catan"
  gameTitle="Catan"
  category="Rules"
  publishDate="2025-05-06"
  updatedDate="2026-10-08"
>
  <p>
    Development cards are Catan's wild cards — powerful, unpredictable, and
    surrounded by timing rules that cause arguments. Here's the complete breakdown.
  </p>

  <KeyTakeaway answer="You can play one development card per turn, at any point in your turn — including before you roll the dice. You can't play a card on the turn you bought it. Victory Point cards are the exception to both rules: they're never 'played', just revealed when they give you 10 points." />

  <h2>Quick Answers</h2>

  <h3>Can you play more than one development card per turn?</h3>
  <p>
    No. You can play only <strong>one</strong> development card per turn — one Knight
    <em>or</em> one progress card (Road Building, Year of Plenty or Monopoly), not
    both. Victory Point cards don't count toward that limit, because they're never
    played; you reveal them when they bring you to 10 points.
  </p>

  <h3>Can you play a development card before rolling the dice?</h3>
  <p>
    Yes. You can play your one development card at any time during your turn,
    <strong>including before you roll</strong>. This matters most with a Knight: play
    it first to move the robber off your best hex, and that hex produces on the
    roll that follows.
  </p>

  <h3>Can you play a development card on the same turn you buy it?</h3>
  <p>
    No. A card bought this turn has to wait until your next turn at the earliest.
    The one exception is a Victory Point card: if the card you just bought takes you
    to 10 points, you reveal it immediately and win.
  </p>

  <h3>Can you play a development card on someone else's turn?</h3>
  <p>
    No. Development cards are only played on your own turn. If the robber lands on
    you during another player's turn, your Knight has to wait until you're up.
  </p>

  <h3>Can you build or trade after playing a development card?</h3>
  <p>
    Yes. Playing a card doesn't end anything — Road Building and Year of Plenty are
    usually played precisely so you can build straight afterwards.
  </p>

